Nurse:
agents: 
  humans: Captain
  robots: Robot1, Robot2
locations: Warehouse, Surface Texturization Start, Surface Texturization End, 
            Lasers Start, Lasers End, Loading Area
resources: RawMaterial
sequences:
  Robot1: 
    1: moveTo Surface Texturization Start
    2: receiveFrom Warehouse RawMaterial
    3: follow Robot2
    4: pick RawMaterial from Surface Texturization End
    5: moveTo Lasers Start
    6: deposit RawMaterial at Lasers Start
    7: receiveFrom Lasers End RawMaterial
    8: pick RawMaterial from Lasers End
    9: moveTo Loading Area
    10: deposit RawMaterial at Loading Area
  Robot2: 
    1: moveTo Surface Texturization End
    2: receiveFrom Surface Texturization Start RawMaterial
    3: follow Robot1
    4: pick RawMaterial from Surface Texturization Start
    5: moveTo Lasers End
    6: deposit RawMaterial at Lasers End
    7: receiverFrom Lasers Start RawMaterial
    8: pick RawMaterial from Lasers Start
    9: moveTo Surface Texturization Start
    10: deposit RawMaterial at Surface Texturization Start
system:
  success: time(10)
  failure:


I will detail how it works:

1. There are two sequences assigned to the two robots (`Robot1`, `Robot2`), and they must see every other one on their own.
2. Each robot takes their respective first resource (`RawMaterial`).
3. Robots ‘Robot1 and ‘Robot2’ should begin to collect their own sequential resource pair after the initial resource move beginning.
4. They are able to advance on the main resource container once transported the `RawMaterial` onto `Surface Texturization`.
